    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31743" root="غرل" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْرَلُ</span></b> , with which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْغَلُ</span> is syn. in all of the
following senses, (TA,) applied to a boy, (S, O.)
<i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أقْلَفُ</span> [i. e. <i>Uncircumcised</i>]: (S, O, Msb, K:)
fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَرْلَآءُ</span>: and pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُرْلٌ</span>. (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْشٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَغْرَلُ</span> <i>A life ample in its means,</i> or <i>circumstances.</i>
(S, O, K.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامٌ أَغْرَلُ</span> <i>A fruitful,</i> or <i>plentiful, year.</i> (K.)

